  "_about": "Per-occurrence shapes for signs whose stone glyph list offers two forms. Key: L<line>:<database symbol>#<nth in line>. glyph: the database glyph id the drawing shows. evidence: drawings consulted (file names on the database). confidence: clear (drawings agree, shape unmistakable), probable (one clear drawing, others damaged or silent), disputed (drawings disagree; the glyph given is the majority or the clearest). direction: 'ltr' when the carver wrote that stretch left to right; the glyph is then the shape as drawn, and the encoder takes its mirror partner. Mirrored glyphs (D04, N04, N05, Y03, S05, Z04, L03, NJ04) encode as the letter they mirror.",
